// Recorded data for the time-series validation and forecasting lesson.
//
// Generated by scripts/verify-timeseries-data.py from the served daily CSV and
// the declared protocol. Every number below was RE-DERIVED there -- the
// baselines by explicit loops, the ridge predictions by standardization written
// from its definition and the normal equations solved by LU -- and then compared
// leaf by leaf with the frozen content packet. Nothing is copied through.
//
// Three kinds of number live here and are labelled wherever the page prints them:
//
//   series      the unchanged recorded daily rental counts and their calendar.
//   development a six-candidate comparison used to SELECT a procedure.
//   final       the locked rolling assessment of the selected procedure and the
//               two predeclared baselines. Not a benchmark, and not a claim
//               about any other city, period or update policy.
//
// No model is fitted in the browser. Do not edit by hand.
